 "overview": {
  "summary": "The instrument's unguarded backplane, and the only assembly in it that carries the ac mains. Section 2-17 lists what is on it: the line-select switches, the line fuse, the power switch, a fibre-optic transmitter (J73) and receiver (J74), and the connectors for the Transformer assembly (A22), the Digital Power Supply (A19), the CPU (A20), the Front Panel (A2), the Rear Panel (A21) and the two 24 V dc chassis fans. Almost the whole parts list is connectors and hardware; the only components on it are two varistors, four resistors, six capacitors, two diodes and four switches. Three things make it worth a troubleshooter's time anyway. It is where the line is switched, fused and tapped for the transformer primary, so a dead instrument is diagnosed here first. Every one of the transformer's twenty-odd secondaries passes through it on the way to A19 and, through P81/P82, to the Analog Motherboard (A3) -- and schematic sheet 2 prints an open-circuit voltage for each of them, which is the only place in the manuals those numbers appear. And it carries the fibre-optic link that is the sole electrical break between the unguarded digital section and the guarded analog section, so a calibrator whose analog half has gone silent may have a fault here rather than anywhere it is pointing.",
  "connectors": "Nineteen. To the Analog Motherboard (A3): P81 and P82, 20-pin, mating with J81/J82 (§2-16). To the Transformer assembly (A22): J13 (10 pin, digital secondaries), J14 (16 pin), J15 (14 pin), J16 (8 pin) and J11 (12 pin, the switched line out to the primary). To the Digital Power Supply (A19): J41, DIN 41612 type C 64-socket. To the CPU (A20): J61 and J62, both DIN 41612 type C 64-socket. To the Front Panel (A2): J21, DIN 41612 type C 64-pin right angle. To the Rear Panel (A21): J91, 34-pin ribbon. To the fans: J51 and J52, 3 pin. To the rear-panel line filter: J31, 5 pin right angle. Fibre optic: J73 transmitter and J74 receiver. There is no A4 equivalent of Table 2-1 -- that table is the Analog Motherboard's -- so the pin-level information exists only on schematic sheets 1 to 3.",
  "source": "§2-16, §2-17, §2-18 and schematic sheets 1–3 of Figure 7-4"
 },
