    "note": "The order matters and it is not the order you would guess. Sheet 1: the line arrives at the rear-panel receptacle, passes through the ac line filter FL1 and the line cord connector P31 — none of which is on this board — and reaches J31, a 5-pin right-angle header. From J31 it goes straight to SW1, the instrument on/off switch, and only then to F1. So SW1 and the tracks between J31 and F1 are live and unfused whenever the line cord is plugged in. RV2 (430 V) is the only component across the line, and it sits downstream of F1; there is no line capacitor on this board, and C5 despite its 250 V ac rating is on sheet 3 and not in the mains path at all. From there SW2, SW3 and SW4 — three DPDT slide switches, drawn as 2P2TSW — select which primary taps the line reaches and hand eight lines (108A, 122A, 8A, 0A, 108B, 122B, 8B, 0B) plus SHIELD to J11 and out to the transformer. The switch table printed on sheet 1 reads RIGHT=0, LEFT=1: 120 V is 0-0-0, 115 V 0-0-1, 110 V 0-1-0, 100 V 0-1-1, 240 V 1-0-0, 230 V 1-0-1, 220 V 1-1-0 and 200 V 1-1-1.",
