    "note": "Sheet 2 is one large interconnect and nothing else: the transformer's secondaries arrive on P13, P14, P15 and P16 and leave on J14, J15, P81 and P82 for the analog assemblies. RV1 (22 V), R4 (68 Ω) and C6 (6800 pF) are the only components on the sheet — a snubber and clamp from the guard node (E2) to earth ground, which is what keeps the guard from being driven by line transients. Sheet 2 prints an open-circuit voltage beside every secondary winding, with the note that they assume a 122 V 60 Hz primary: 12.9 V + 12.9 V and 39.5 V on S1; 82.9 V and 8.3 V on S2; 25.1 V + 25.1 V and 14.4 V + 14.4 V on S3; 428.4 V / 214.2 V / 55.6 V / 55.6 V / 214.2 V / 428.4 V on S4; and 20.1 V + 20.1 V, 39.5 V, 10.1 V, 11.5 V, 23 V and 39.5 V on S5. The 428 V taps are why P81, P82 and J15 carry WARNING HIGH VOLTAGE on the silkscreen.",
