    "note": "The four secondaries A19 runs on arrive together on J13, a 10-pin header, and go straight out on J41 to A19 with no component of any kind in between — which is what makes J13 and J41 the two places to measure when the instrument will not boot. Sheet 3 prints both pin maps in full. J13: pin 1 and 2 are 5 AC 1/2, pin 3 is unused, pins 4 and 5 are 75 AC 1/2, pins 6 and 7 are 35 AC 1/2, and pins 8, 9 and 10 are 12 AC 1, 12 AC CT and 12 AC 2. J41 doubles most of them across its A and C rows: 5 AC 1 on 1A/2A/1C/2C, 5 AC 2 on 3A/4A/3C/4C, 75 AC 1 on 7A/7C, 75 AC 2 on 8A/8C, 35 AC 1 on 9A/9C, 35 AC 2 on 10A/10C, 12 AC 1 on 11A/12A/11C, 12 AC CT on 13A/14A/13C and 12 AC 2 on 15A/16A/15C. A19's regulated rails come back the same way — +35 V on 18A/18C, +12V FAN on 20A/20C, +12 V on 21A/21C, −12 V on 26A/26C, −12V FAN on 27A/27C, +5 V on 32A/32C and +75 V on 24A/24C — along with PSFAILINTR* on 5A, 75VSD on 5C and RESETL on 29C.",
