    "note": "The only place on this board where a passive component does something other than sit across a line. Each fan runs from +12V FAN to −12V FAN, 24 V across it, through a 2 Ω wirewound sense resistor — R2 for fan 1 into J51, R3 for fan 2 into J52. The voltage across each resistor is the analog signal FAN1 or FAN2, which goes to the CPU on J61 and is what §2-45's fan monitor compares: U52D on A20 subtracts one from the other, and a window comparator raises FANINT* if either fan is shorted, open or drawing too much. So a fan fault reported by the instrument is measured here and judged there. C1 and C4 (10 µF) bypass each fan line and CR3 and CR4 (1N4002) are across them. Both fans are labelled NOT ON MOTHERBOARD on sheet 3: J51 and J52 are the headers, P51 and P52 the plugs on the fan leads.",
