   "note": "10 uF 35 V tantalum, polarity marked + on the +12V FAN side. Sheet 3 shows it connected between the +12V FAN line and the -12V FAN line on the supply side of the 2 ohm sense resistor R2, so it sees the whole 24 V the fan runs on rather than one 12 V rail. 24 V on a 35 V part is 69% of rating -- high for a solid tantalum by modern practice, normal for 1987, and comfortably the most stressed capacitor on this assembly. Both rails come from A19's U1 and U2 through J41 pins 20A/20C and 27A/27C; Table 2-2 gives them as +12 V and -12 V."
